Subject: fix: free buildHexData buffer in EurekaScalesPlugin::handles (per-advertisement heap leak)

EurekaScalesPlugin::handles() calls NimBLEUtils::buildHexData(nullptr, ...), which
malloc's a length*2+1 byte buffer and transfers ownership to the caller. The buffer is
copied into a std::string but never freed, so every BLE advertisement evaluated by the
Eureka plugin during scanning leaks a small allocation. RemoteScalesScanner scans
continuously (start(0)), so on an ESP32-S3 display board left out of standby for hours
the leak accumulates one block per ambient advertisement until the heap is exhausted,
AsyncTCP can no longer allocate connection buffers, and the web UI becomes unreachable
until reboot.

Fix: free the buffer after copying it, and guard the (rare) malloc-failure case to
avoid constructing std::string from a null pointer.

This patch targets gaggimate/esp-arduino-ble-scales (base commit 46bae8c) and is applied
at build time by scripts/patch_ble_scales.py until it lands upstream and the dependency
is re-pinned to the merged commit.
---
diff --git a/src/scales/eureka.h b/src/scales/eureka.h
index 7db1c95..f0880b0 100644
--- a/src/scales/eureka.h
+++ b/src/scales/eureka.h
@@ -55,7 +55,11 @@ private:
     }
     const std::string& deviceData = device.getManufacturerData();
     char *pHex = NimBLEUtils::buildHexData(nullptr, (uint8_t*) deviceData.c_str(), deviceData.length());
+    if (pHex == nullptr) {
+      return false;
+    }
     std::string md(pHex);
+    free(pHex); // buildHexData(target=nullptr,...) malloc's and transfers ownership; must free or it leaks per advertisement
     return !md.empty() && deviceName.empty() && (md.find("a6bc") != std::string::npos || md.find("042") == 0);
   }
 };
